 "result_text": "The issue asks for new unit tests, but you told me to change source only, so I didn't write any tests. While reading the uncovered lines I found three bugs and fixed them. The existing tests still pass (17 passed). I didn't run coverage or add tests for the new paths.\n\n- **`tes/models.py`, `Task.is_valid`:** `for k, v in e.env` and `for k, v in self.tags` iterated over dict keys rather than items, so validation would fail or misbehave whenever env or tags were set. I changed both to `.items()`.\n- **`tes/models.py`, same two checks:** the string check tested `k` twice (`not isinstance(k, str) and not isinstance(k, str)`), so values were never checked. It now rejects a non-string key or a non-string value.\n- **`tes/client.py`, `wait`:** the `TimeoutError` message was missing its `f` prefix, so it printed `{response.as_dict()}` literally. I added it.\n\nI left `tes/utils.py` alone. Its uncovered lines look like error paths that only need tests, not code changes.",
